  "decision": "Retain baseline compensation until loop redesign is justified. Smaller compensation worsens excursions and can leave sustained oscillation; larger compensation and a 10ns load ramp each reduce excursions but do not close the dynamic error. No new capacitor geometry or ramp implementation is adopted.",
  "next_action": "Measure loaded loop response and evaluate local output-stage feedback or explicit controlled current turn-on/off. Preserve sustained drive and all power-state requirements.",
  "scope": "Standalone ideal current sink/source includes a +/-24mA reversal, more adverse than ordinary unidirectional TX supply loading; use retained-pad lifecycle for actual capability decisions. Ramp changes current demand only, not serial data edge rate."
